---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Rules" description="Glitched Network server rules.">
    <main class="legal-page">
        <article>
            <h1 class="font-PressStart2P">Rules</h1>
            <p>These are the main community rules and the in-game server rules for Glitched SMP.</p>

            <h2>Main Rules</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Respectful Behavior:</strong> No homophobic, discriminatory, or offensive language. Be respectful to everyone at all times.</li>
                <li><strong>No Spamming:</strong> Avoid using all caps excessively or sending rapid messages in a short period of time.</li>
                <li><strong>No Loopholing:</strong> Trying to bypass or technically break the rules is still breaking the rules.</li>
                <li><strong>Language Use:</strong> Swearing is allowed in moderation, but not when directed at others. For example, saying "F cancer" is fine, but not "F you."</li>
                <li><strong>Staff Decisions:</strong> Staff always have the final say. If you believe a staff member is abusing their power, use /report or message a higher-up, such as a Mod, Admin, Sr. Admin, Staff Manager, Co-owner, or Owner.</li>
                <li><strong>Common Decency:</strong> Just because something is not written here does not mean it is allowed. NSFW content is never allowed.</li>
                <li><strong>No DM Advertising:</strong> Do not promote servers or services through DMs. It will result in a ban.</li>
                <li><strong>No Harassment:</strong> Do not insult, bully, or harass anyone in chat, voice, or DMs. Friendly jokes are fine, but know the line.</li>
                <li><strong>Don't Be a Jerk:</strong> Treat others how you would want to be treated. This is a community, not a competition.</li>
                <li><strong>Suspicious/NSFW Links:</strong> Do not send or click suspicious or NSFW links. You will be held responsible.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Server Rules</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Main Rules Apply:</strong> All rules above are also enforced in-game.</li>
                <li><strong>No Hacked Clients or Exploits:</strong> Using any form of hack, exploit, or cheat is strictly prohibited.</li>
                <li><strong>Respect Others:</strong> Treat other players fairly. Harassment, bullying, or targeting is not tolerated.</li>
                <li><strong>Be Responsible:</strong> If you are involved in a dispute or incident, act maturely and responsibly.</li>
                <li><strong>No Lag/Crash Attempts:</strong> Intentionally trying to lag or crash the server is a bannable offense.</li>
                <li><strong>Vanilla Enchant Limits Only:</strong> Do not use enchantments above Minecraft's default cap.</li>
                <li><strong>Enchants Above Default Levels:</strong> Enchant levels up to 7 were previously allowed, but this has changed. Only default vanilla levels are now permitted. If you have an overpowered enchant, report it to a Mod, Admin, or Developer. If you are caught using one without reporting it, your inventory will be wiped with no questions asked.</li>
                <li><strong>No Heavy Griefing or Stealing:</strong> Minor mischief is okay. However, actions like lava cascades, farming players, or large-scale griefing are not allowed.</li>
                <li><strong>Advertising Rules:</strong> In-game advertising of server-related content, like shops or services, is fine. Do not advertise other servers in chat or on signs.</li>
                <li><strong>English Only in Public Chat:</strong> Please keep public messages in English for moderation clarity.</li>
                <li><strong>No Bug/Glitch Abuse:</strong> If you find a glitch, report it. Using it for personal gain is a punishable offense.</li>
                <li><strong>No Begging:</strong> Do not beg for items, staff help, or favors.</li>
                <li><strong>No Mod Requests:</strong> Mods are not being added. Please do not ask.</li>
                <li><strong>Inventory Rollbacks:</strong> Rollbacks are only possible if the death was caused by a bug or glitch and evidence is provided.</li>
                <li><strong>Staff Material Requests:</strong> Do not ask staff to give or replace your items unless it is verified by logs or proof.</li>
                <li><strong>No AFK Killing:</strong> Do not kill players while they are AFK. Check the TAB menu or punch them first. If they do not respond, they are AFK.</li>
            </ol>
        </article>
    </main>
</MainLayout>
